\DOC LOCAL_JADD_SAFETY_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_JADD_SAFETY_TAC : string -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Steps an {eventually}-style goal across one subroutine call by applying a named
assumed callee specification, replacing the facts about the current symbolic
state with facts about its successor and leaving one subgoal.

\DESCRIBE
{assump_name : string} is the label of the assumption in the goal carrying the
callee's specification to be applied; {n : int} is the index of the current
symbolic state, used to name the states in the resulting assumptions, the
successor being indexed {n+1}. The conclusion retains the shape
{eventually ... s'}, with only the final state argument advancing from the
state numbered {n} to the one numbered {n+1}. Among the assumptions, every fact
mentioning the old state — program loaded, register/flag and memory reads, the
accumulated event trace, and the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation from the
initial state — is discarded and replaced by the corresponding fact about the
new state, where the event trace is extended by the callee's trace function and
the {MAYCHANGE} relation is extended with the callee's clobbered footprint. Two
further assumptions appear: an equation defining a freshly named trace variable
as the callee's event function applied to the call's arguments, and a
memory-access-in-bounds fact about that variable. The named specification
assumption, together with the other assumed specifications, stays available,
although the assumption list may be reordered. Exactly one subgoal results.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the tactic performs this same single-step
transformation on goals whose assumptions include such callee specifications
and a symbolic machine state.

\ENDDOC
